@@ -29,3 +29,14 @@ applyPatch({ a: 1 }, [{ op: "add", path: "/b", value: 2 }]); // { a: 1, b: 2 }
 `applyPatch(document, patch)` applies the operations (`add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, `test`) in
 order and returns a new document; inputs are never mutated. It throws an `Error` if the patch is invalid or
 any operation fails.
+
+## JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)
+
+```ts
+import { applyMergePatch } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+applyMergePatch({ a: "b", c: 1 }, { a: null, d: 2 }); // { c: 1, d: 2 }
+```
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` merges an object patch recursively (`null` removes a member); any non-object
+patch, including arrays, replaces the target. Inputs are never mutated. It does not throw.
